        <name>Aligned and dose weighted micrographs of mouse apoferritin sorted by ice thickness collected on a 200 kV Glacios microscope with a Falcon3 detector in integrating mode</name>
        <directory>/data/22feb15b-Glacios_Falcon3_integrating</directory>
        <category>micrographs - single frame</category>
        <headerFormat>MRC</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>MRC</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>3474</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>1</framesPerImage>
        <voxelType>32 BIT FLOAT</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>4096</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>1.204</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>4096</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>1.204</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>Micrographs were aligned and dose weighted in MotionCor2. Here, they have been sorted into their respective ice thickness bins, 0-50 nm, 50-100 nm, 100-150 nm, 150-200 nm, and 200-500 nm. The obj_icegraph.txt file lists all micrographs collected during the session and the corresponding ice thickness measured by aperture limited scattering.</details>
